## 8. Limitations
- ROI coordinates are tuned for a forward-facing viewpoint.
- Hough parameters are fixed.
- Intensity-based candidates can confuse shadows with surface defects.
- The perspective model is approximate.
- The system does not semantically classify road damage.
- It is a Computer Vision demonstration, not an autonomous-driving safety system.

## 9. Future Scope
Automatic ROI estimation, lane polynomial fitting, vanishing-point detection, video temporal filtering, camera calibration, labelled defect evaluation.

## 10. Conclusion
The project integrates preprocessing, edge information, geometric detection, morphology and projective transformation into one reproducible classical Computer Vision workflow. The intermediate outputs make the effect of each stage directly inspectable, while the numerical summary supports quantitative comparison.
